# Rank 1591 / CVE-2026-42810: Apache Polaris built its delegated
# access policies from granted storage paths used as raw string
# prefixes, so a grant on one path also authorized sibling paths
# sharing it as a text prefix -- in the S3 IAM variant, literal *
# characters accepted in table names reappeared unescaped in
# resource patterns and matched other tables' locations; in the GCS
# variant, a grant on "data" satisfied startsWith conditions for
# "data_foo/*" (policy prefix-match bypass, CWE-284/CWE-80). The
# GCS downscoping in
# polaris-core/src/main/java/org/apache/polaris/core/storage/gcp/
# GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration.java fed `String path =
# uri.rawPath().substring(1)` into resourceNameStartsWith and
# objectListPrefixStartsWith CEL conditions with no segment
# boundary. POOL CORRECTION applied in place: the row held
# da54eb15c2 (a documentation-wording commit); the verifiable fix
# is d9731452, "Fix GCS credential downscoping path traversal /
# prefix match bypass (#4884)" -- every granted path passes through
# StorageLocation.ensureTrailingSlash before entering the
# conditions, so "data/" can no longer authorize "data_foo/*" (the
# S3 twin, escapeIamGlobLiteral escaping * ? $ into IAM variable
# syntax, shipped in the same class of change). No further pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, policy-prefix semantics. The guard (location
# allowlisting) exists -- the defect is that a string prefix is not
# a path segment: siblings sharing the text prefix match, the same
# prefix-vs-structure family as rank 1583 (URL userinfo against a
# prefix allowlist). Nothing can ask "does this policy condition
# compare path segments rather than string prefixes" -- that is
# storage-policy vocabulary. A binding on Polaris's own
# integrations would detect this platform rather than the weakness.
# Measured on the real code: scanning the GCS integration reports
# zero findings at both revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1591 records the raw
# prefix grant and the trailing-slash form, both asserting reject
# VYQL-AUTH-079: when policy-segment vocabulary lands, the raw
# prefix form must flip to expect.

test "rank1591: the granted path is used as a raw prefix"
  lang java
  file polaris-core/src/main/java/org/apache/polaris/core/storage/gcp/GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  import java.util.LinkedHashSet;
  import java.util.Map;

  public class GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration {
      private final Map<String, LinkedHashSet<String>> readConditionsByBucket = new java.util.HashMap<>();

      public void addReadCondition(String location) {
          StorageUri uri = StorageUri.parse(location);
          String bucket = uri.authority();
          String path = uri.rawPath().substring(1);
          readConditionsByBucket
              .computeIfAbsent(bucket, key -> new LinkedHashSet<>())
              .add(resourceNameStartsWithExpression(bucket, path));
      }

      String resourceNameStartsWithExpression(String bucket, String path) {
          return "resource.name.startsWith('buckets/" + bucket + "/objects/" + path + "')";
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1591: the fix forces a segment boundary"
  lang java
  file polaris-core/src/main/java/org/apache/polaris/core/storage/gcp/GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  import java.util.LinkedHashSet;
  import java.util.Map;

  public class GcpCredentialsStorageIntegration {
      private final Map<String, LinkedHashSet<String>> readConditionsByBucket = new java.util.HashMap<>();

      public void addReadCondition(String location) {
          StorageUri uri = StorageUri.parse(location);
          String bucket = uri.authority();
          // Treat the granted path as a directory prefix: a trailing slash is required so
          // that the downstream startsWith() CEL conditions cannot be satisfied by sibling
          // objects that merely share the granted path as a string prefix.
          String path = StorageLocation.ensureTrailingSlash(uri.rawPath().substring(1));
          readConditionsByBucket
              .computeIfAbsent(bucket, key -> new LinkedHashSet<>())
              .add(resourceNameStartsWithExpression(bucket, path));
      }

      String resourceNameStartsWithExpression(String bucket, String path) {
          return "resource.name.startsWith('buckets/" + bucket + "/objects/" + path + "')";
      }
  }
  ```
